  "source_inspection": {
    "java": [
      "CommandFactoryNote uses quarkInContext(false, cleanId(alias)) and rejects alias reuse only when the selected quark already has data, so named notes live on ordinary quarks in the shared namespace.",
      "CommandLinkClass uses quarkInContextSafe(true, endpoint) for both endpoints; if the selected note quark already holds NOTE data, no phantom CLASS is created and the Link keeps the note entity itself.",
      "EntityImageNote serializes data-qualified-name directly from getEntity().getQuark().getQualifiedName(), so custom namespace separators survive into SVG first and are only later punctuation-translated by the SVG writer."
    ],
    "rust": [
      "push_note now registers note_by_path on the current-context quark path and stores a canonical note.id, which fixes the earlier phantom-class path for root and reopened-package notes.",
      "materialize_relationship_endpoint consults note_by_path before package/entity fallback, so relationships reuse the named note instead of synthesizing a CLASS endpoint in the five passing controls.",
      "note_qualified_name still rebuilds a package-owned floating note name as package_qualified_name(owner) + '.' + translate_qualified_name(leaf). That discards separator characters present in note.id, unlike class entities whose namespaced branch returns translate_qualified_name(entity.id)."
    ]
  },
